{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "vrun-ctw-sms",
  "title": "VRUN CTW (the Corrupt The World demake) on the Master System (S2)",
  "family": "vrun",
  "kind": "sms",
  "console": "sms",
  "description": "The Master System port of VRUN CTW, the NES demake (docs/projects/sega-vrun-ports-plan.md, S2: the view kept in 256x192, the HUD shrinks, PSG sound from the NES version). Today the S0 skeleton: a hello ROM (text, a frame counter, a cursor that Left / Right move) that proves the toolchain and BrokenDev's build / verify / compat. Built with SDCC 4.6.0 + devkitSMS (toolchains.json) in its live workspace PROJECTS/VRUN_CTW_SMS_dev (its own git, local only).",
  "source": {
    "folder": "{live:VRUN_CTW_SMS_dev}"
  },
  "requires": {
    "tools": [
      "ps5",
      "toolchain:sdcc",
      "toolchain:devkitsms"
    ],
    "projects": [],
    "inputs": [],
    "toolchain": [
      "SDCC 4.6.0 and devkitSMS 533ae57, pinned in toolchains.json (SMSlib and crt0 rebuilt from devkitSMS's sources by build.ps1)"
    ]
  },
  "build": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "name": "build",
        "shell": "ps5",
        "cwd": "{src}",
        "file": "{src}/build.ps1",
        "args": [
          "-Sdcc",
          "{toolchain:sdcc}",
          "-DevkitSms",
          "{toolchain:devkitsms}"
        ],
        "timeoutSec": 900,
        "note": "build.ps1: SMSlib and crt0 rebuilt once (build/smslib-sms), sdcc -mz80, makesms; checks 'TMR SEGA' and the Master System export region code (4)."
      }
    ],
    "outputs": [
      {
        "id": "rom",
        "path": "{src}/build/vrun_ctw_sms.sms",
        "publishAs": "vrun_ctw_sms.sms",
        "kind": "sms"
      },
      {
        "id": "noi",
        "path": "{src}/build/vrun_ctw_sms.noi",
        "publishAs": "vrun_ctw_sms.noi",
        "kind": "symbols"
      },
      {
        "id": "sym",
        "path": "{src}/build/vrun_ctw_sms.sym",
        "publishAs": "vrun_ctw_sms.sym",
        "kind": "symbols-wla"
      },
      {
        "id": "map",
        "path": "{src}/build/vrun_ctw_sms.map",
        "publishAs": "vrun_ctw_sms.map",
        "kind": "map"
      }
    ]
  },
  "run": {
    "console": "sms",
    "note": "The skeleton: Left / Right move the cursor. Lite: the .sms opens in BrokenNes Lite's Master System (UAT/entrypoints/lite-sega.ps1 -Roms <folder with sms\\vrun_ctw_sms.sms>)."
  },
  "verify": {
    "timeoutSec": 600,
    "scenarios": [
      {
        "id": "play",
        "frames": 700,
        "input": "120:B,132:,400:Right",
        "checkpoints": [
          100,
          380,
          700
        ],
        "expect": {
          "minDistinctColors": 4,
          "pictureDiffers": [
            100,
            380
          ],
          "memory": [
            {
              "symbol": "_app_state",
              "is": 1,
              "what": "the title's B started a game (APP_GAME)"
            },
            {
              "symbol": "_current_room",
              "is": 0,
              "what": "still in the first room"
            },
            {
              "symbol": "_player_hp",
              "is": 5,
              "what": "full health"
            }
          ]
        },
        "why": "the game boots to the title, B starts a run and the first room plays (the S0 hello scenario is gone)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "compat": {
    "what": "The game on every Master System emulator BrokenDev has, from power-on and the same pad script (B on the title, then Right), its state read by the build's symbols every frame.",
    "symbols": {
      "file": "{out}/vrun_ctw_sms.noi"
    },
    "reads": {
      "frame": "_nmi_counter",
      "state": "_app_state",
      "room": "_current_room"
    },
    "frameTolerance": 30,
    "scenarios": [
      {
        "id": "play",
        "frames": 700,
        "input": "120:B,132:,400:Right",
        "shots": [
          100,
          700
        ],
        "what": "power-on, the title, B starts a run, Right walks in the first room",
        "checks": [
          {
            "id": "alive",
            "what": "the frame interrupt runs (nmi_counter keeps changing)",
            "changes": "frame",
            "within": [
              60,
              700
            ],
            "min": 200
          },
          {
            "id": "started",
            "what": "B on the title started a game",
            "read": "state",
            "is": 1,
            "within": [
              200,
              700
            ],
            "hold": true
          },
          {
            "id": "room0",
            "what": "the first room",
            "read": "room",
            "is": 0,
            "within": [
              200,
              700
            ],
            "hold": true
          },
          {
            "id": "drawn",
            "what": "the room is drawn",
            "picture": 700,
            "minColors": 4
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "comparison": {
    "what": "S2: the Master System port against VRUN CTW on the NES (project vrun-nes-mmc3, the MMC3 main build: since 2026-11-10 the port is translated from main.fab + mapper_mmc3.fab). The port is the same game code translated to C (tools/fab2c.py), so the tolerance is the plan's 'same events, small drift': rooms, items, deaths in the same order, positions within 4 pixels. Both sides 60 Hz, one tick a frame, time 0 = the first frame of the game (app_state 1). NESFab keeps each byte of a variable apart (player_x@1 = the whole pixel), the port's C variables are 8.8 fixed point (byte +1 = the pixel).",
    "original": "vrun-nes-mmc3",
    "rate": {
      "original": {
        "fps": 60,
        "origin": "state=1",
        "tick": "{run_timer@0} * 60 + [run_timer_subsec@0]"
      },
      "port": {
        "fps": 60,
        "origin": "state=1",
        "tick": "{_run_timer} * 60 + [_run_timer_subsec]"
      }
    },
    "input": "used",
    "padVars": {
      "Right": "move_right@0",
      "Left": "move_left@0",
      "Up": "move_up@0",
      "Down": "move_down@0",
      "A": "jump_held@0",
      "B": "fire_held@0"
    },
    "padWhen": "state=1",
    "tolerance": {
      "ticks": 6,
      "positions": 4
    },
    "sampleEveryTicks": 10,
    "variables": [
      {
        "name": "state",
        "kind": "event",
        "original": "app_state@0",
        "port": "_app_state"
      },
      {
        "name": "room",
        "kind": "event",
        "original": "current_room@0",
        "port": "_current_room"
      },
      {
        "name": "map",
        "kind": "event",
        "original": "map_slot@0",
        "port": "_map_slot"
      },
      {
        "name": "hp",
        "kind": "event",
        "original": "player_hp@0",
        "port": "_player_hp"
      },
      {
        "name": "cash",
        "kind": "event",
        "original": "le16 score@0",
        "port": "le16 _score"
      },
      {
        "name": "x",
        "kind": "position",
        "original": "player_x@1",
        "port": "[_player_x + 1]"
      },
      {
        "name": "y",
        "kind": "position",
        "original": "player_y@1",
        "port": "[_player_y + 1]"
      }
    ],
    "buttons": {
      "A": "B",
      "B": "A",
      "Start": "B"
    },
    "settleFrames": 122,
    "play": {
      "what": "D1 (Timeflow T6): brokendev.ps1 timeflow play-compare vrun-ctw-sms. The NES original (the MMC3 main build, ./build.sh game --mmc3; 2026-11-10, was mapper 30) built from a git archive of VRUN at a36dd5e (bends + duty translated since 783c093), and the port translated from that same tree (build.ps1 -FabRoot), both into C:\\BrokenNes-work\\play-compare (the shipping builds are not touched); the seed is the title's frame count (the map slot), fixed by Start at frame 120. Then a scripted walk out of room 0 (right, firing, a jump: room 1 at about frame 700) and a seeded walker (tools/playscript.py --from 770 --seed 3 --buttons A,B) that jumps and fires: rooms, hits, cash. The NES build's tools need Python 3.12+ (py -3.14). 2026-11-10 (the MMC3 original): the whole script is 11 frames earlier (Start at 109: map slot 11, the mapper-30 script's map): the MMC3 build reaches its title 10 frames before mapper 30 (ledger row 55), so the same walk meets the same map.",
